            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856",
              "name": "CVE-2026-11856",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin\n(`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a\ndifferent one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes\nlibcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`,\nto `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-11856",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8925",
              "name": "CVE-2026-8925",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8925 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The curl logic that works with SASL authentication could end up cleaning up\nthe GSASL context *twice* without clearing the pointer in between, making it\n`free()` the same pointer twice."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8925",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9079",
              "name": "CVE-2026-9079",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9079 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl had a flaw that when instructed to clear proxy authentication\ncredentials which made it not do so, leaving the old credentials around to get\nused for subsequent transfers that should not know nor use them."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-9079",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8924",
              "name": "CVE-2026-8924",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8924 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in curl’s cookie parsing logic allows a malicious HTTP server to set\n'super cookies' that bypass the Public Suffix List check. This enables an\nattacker-controlled origin to inject cookies that curl subsequently scopes and\ntransmits to unrelated third-party domains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8924",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-10536",
              "name": "CVE-2026-10536",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-10536 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application\nconfigures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or\n`CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and\nfinally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final\ncleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure\nthat was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-10536",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8927",
              "name": "CVE-2026-8927",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8927 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When reusing a libcurl handle for sequential transfers driven by\nenvironment-variable proxy configuration, libcurl fails to clear the proxy\nauthentication state between requests. Specifically, if the initial transfer\nauthenticates against `proxyA` using Digest auth, a subsequent transfer routed\nthrough `proxyB` erroneously leaks the `Proxy-Authorization:` header intended\nsolely for `proxyA`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8927",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8926",
              "name": "CVE-2026-8926",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8926 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When asking curl to use a `.netrc` file to find credentials and at the same\ntime specifying a URL with a username(without a password), like\n`https://user@example.com/`, curl could wrongly get and use the password for\n*another* user set in the `.netrc` file for that host if such a one exists and\nthere is no match for the specified user."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8926",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11564",
              "name": "CVE-2026-11564",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11564 in curl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl keeps previously used connections in a connection pool for subsequent\ntransfers to reuse if one of them matches the setup.\n\nAn easy handle that first uses default native CA trust can continue trusting\nthe native platform store after the application switches that same handle to\ncustom CA material for a later transfer."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-11564",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-40962",
              "name": "CVE-2026-40962",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-40962 in ffmpeg"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "FFmpeg before 8.1 has an integer overflow and resultant out-of-bounds write via CENC (Common Encryption) subsample data to libavformat/mov.c."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-40962",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42216",
              "name": "CVE-2026-42216",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42216 in libopenexr-3-1-30"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. From versions 3.0.0 to before 3.2.9, 3.3.0 to before 3.3.11, and 3.4.0 to before 3.4.11, IDManifest::init() reconstructs strings from a prefix-compressed representation. If the previous string is longer than 255 bytes, the next string is expected to begin with a 2-byte prefix length. The code reads stringList[i][0] and stringList[i][1] without checking that the current string has at least two bytes. This issue has been patched in versions 3.2.9, 3.3.11, and 3.4.11."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42216",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42217",
              "name": "CVE-2026-42217",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42217 in libopenexr-3-1-30"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. From versions 3.0.0 to before 3.2.9, 3.3.0 to before 3.3.11, and 3.4.0 to before 3.4.11, readVariableLengthInteger() decodes a variable-length integer from untrusted EXR input without bounding the shift count. After enough continuation bytes, the code executes a left shift by 70 on a 64-bit value, which is undefined behavior. This issue has been patched in versions 3.2.9, 3.3.11, and 3.4.11."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42217",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41242",
              "name": "CVE-2026-41242",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41242 in protobufjs"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "protobufjs compiles protobuf definitions into JavaScript (JS) functions. In versions prior to 8.0.1 and 7.5.5, attackers can inject arbitrary code in the \"type\" fields of protobuf definitions, which will then execute during object decoding using that definition. Versions 8.0.1 and 7.5.5 patch the issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41242",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "critical"
                ]
              }
            },
