                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-37555",
              "name": "CVE-2026-37555",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-37555 in libsndfile1"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in libsndfile 1.2.2 IMA ADPCM codec. The AIFF code path (line 241) was fixed with (sf_count_t) cast, but the WAV code path (line 235) and close path (line 167) were not. When samplesperblock (int) * blocks (int) exceeds INT_MAX, the 32-bit multiplication overflows before being assigned to sf.frames (sf_count_t/int64). With samplesperblock=50000 and blocks=50000, the product 2500000000 overflows to -1794967296. This causes incorrect frame count leading to heap buffer overflow or denial of service. Both values come from the WAV file header and are attacker-controlled. This issue was discovered after an incomplete fix for CVE-2022-33065."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-37555",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55199",
              "name": "CVE-2026-55199",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-55199 in libssh2-1"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit 1762685, contains a pre-authentication denial of service vulnerability in the SSH_MSG_EXT_INFO handler in src/packet.c that allows a malicious SSH server to cause a client CPU exhaustion loop by sending a crafted extension count value. A malicious server can set nr_extensions to 0xFFFFFFFF during key exchange, causing the client to spin in a tight CPU loop for over 60 seconds because return values from _libssh2_get_string() are unchecked and the session timeout does not apply to CPU-bound loops."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55199",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55200",
              "name": "CVE-2026-55200",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-55200 in libssh2-1"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit 7acf3df contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in ssh2_transport_read() that fails to enforce upper bounds on packet_length field. Remote attackers can send crafted SSH packets with excessively large packet_length values to corrupt heap memory and achieve remote code execution."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55200",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7598",
              "name": "CVE-2026-7598",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7598 in libssh2-1"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A security vulnerability has been detected in libssh2 up to 1.11.1. The impacted element is the function userauth_password of the file src/userauth.c. Such manipulation of the argument username_len/password_len leads to integer overflow. The attack may be launched remotely. The name of the patch is 256d04b60d80bf1190e96b0ad1e91b2174d744b1. A patch should be applied to remediate this issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-7598",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
