                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50256",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50256",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50256 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A stack-based buffer overflow flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland. A mismatch between the X server and the libXfont2 library's maximum font name length can cause a stack buffer overflow during font alias resolution. The server allocates a 256 byte stack buffer but libXfont2's alias target name length is 1024 bytes. A font alias name between 257 and 1023 bytes causes the X server to copy that name into the undersized stack buffer without further checks. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50256",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50257",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50257",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50257 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland in miSyncDestroyFence(). A client that sets up multiple fence triggers can trigger a use-after-free function pointer call. An attacker would connect to the X server to set up a fence and await that fence, then a second X connection destroys the fence, causing the use-after-free. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50257",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50258",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50258",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50258 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A stack-based buffer overflow flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland. The X server has multiple stack buffers sized XkbMaxShiftLevel * XkbNumKbdGroups but CheckKeyTypes() does not verify or clamp non-canonical key types to XkbMaxShiftLevel. A client can change key types to excessive shift levels and trigger stack overflows. This is caused by an incomplete fix of CVE-2025-26597. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50258",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50259",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50259",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50259 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A stack-based buffer overflow flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland. _XkbSetMapChecks() declares a fixed-size stack buffer mapWidths[256] indexed by key type index. The helper function CheckKeyTypes() writes to this buffer at a client-controlled offset, allowing a stack buffer overflow. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50259",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50260",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50260",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50260 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland in FreeCounter(). A client that sets up multiple SyncCounters and awaits on those triggers can trigger a use-after-free when destroying those counters via a second client connection. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50260",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50261",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50261",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50261 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland in SyncChangeCounter(). A client that sets up multiple SyncCounters can trigger a use-after-free when destroying those counters via a second client connection while changing those counters. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50261",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50264",
              "name": "CVE-2026-50264",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-50264 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An out-of-bounds write flaw was found in the X.Org X server and Xwayland in DRIGetBuffers/DRIGetBuffersWithFormat. A client that requests multiple DRI2BufferBackLeft attachments and one DRI2BufferFrontLeft can trigger an out-of-bounds heap write. This may be used to crash the server, or for privilege escalation if the X server runs as root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50264",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55999",
              "name": "CVE-2026-55999",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-55999 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Local attackers with a X connection able to provide PCX fonts to the X \nserver xorg-server before 21.2.24 and xwayland before 24.1.13 could \ncause a heap buffer overflow via SetFont due to missing glyph boundary checks."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55999",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "high"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56000",
              "name": "CVE-2026-56000",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56000 in xserver-common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Local attackers with a X connection able to provide GLX commit to the X server xorg-server before 21.2.24 and xwayland before 24.1.13 could cause a Heap Use After Free, due to CommonMakeCurrent() pointing into potentially reallocated memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56000",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
