                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29406",
              "name": "CVE-2023-29406",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29406 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP/1 client does not fully validate the contents of the Host header. A maliciously crafted Host header can inject additional headers or entire requests. With fix, the HTTP/1 client now refuses to send requests containing an invalid Request.Host or Request.URL.Host value."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-29406",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29409",
              "name": "CVE-2023-29409",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29409 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Extremely large RSA keys in certificate chains can cause a client/server to expend significant CPU time verifying signatures. With fix, the size of RSA keys transmitted during handshakes is restricted to <= 8192 bits. Based on a survey of publicly trusted RSA keys, there are currently only three certificates in circulation with keys larger than this, and all three appear to be test certificates that are not actively deployed. It is possible there are larger keys in use in private PKIs, but we target the web PKI, so causing breakage here in the interests of increasing the default safety of users of crypto/tls seems reasonable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-29409",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39318",
              "name": "CVE-2023-39318",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39318 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The html/template package does not properly handle HTML-like \"\" comment tokens, nor hashbang \"#!\" comment tokens, in <script> contexts. This may cause the template parser to improperly interpret the contents of <script> contexts, causing actions to be improperly escaped. This may be leveraged to perform an XSS attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-39318",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39319",
              "name": "CVE-2023-39319",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39319 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The html/template package does not apply the proper rules for handling occurrences of \"<script\", \"<!--\", and \"</script\" within JS literals in <script> contexts. This may cause the template parser to improperly consider script contexts to be terminated early, causing actions to be improperly escaped. This could be leveraged to perform an XSS attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-39319",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39326",
              "name": "CVE-2023-39326",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39326 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A malicious HTTP sender can use chunk extensions to cause a receiver reading from a request or response body to read many more bytes from the network than are in the body. A malicious HTTP client can further exploit this to cause a server to automatically read a large amount of data (up to about 1GiB) when a handler fails to read the entire body of a request. Chunk extensions are a little-used HTTP feature which permit including additional metadata in a request or response body sent using the chunked encoding. The net/http chunked encoding reader discards this metadata. A sender can exploit this by inserting a large metadata segment with each byte transferred. The chunk reader now produces an error if the ratio of real body to encoded bytes grows too small."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-39326",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45284",
              "name": "CVE-2023-45284",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45284 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Windows, The IsLocal function does not correctly detect reserved device names in some cases. Reserved names followed by spaces, such as \"COM1 \", and reserved names \"COM\" and \"LPT\" followed by superscript 1, 2, or 3, are incorrectly reported as local. With fix, IsLocal now correctly reports these names as non-local."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-45284",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45289",
              "name": "CVE-2023-45289",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45289 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When following an HTTP redirect to a domain which is not a subdomain match or exact match of the initial domain, an http.Client does not forward sensitive headers such as \"Authorization\" or \"Cookie\". For example, a redirect from foo.com to www.foo.com will forward the Authorization header, but a redirect to bar.com will not. A maliciously crafted HTTP redirect could cause sensitive headers to be unexpectedly forwarded."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-45289",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45290",
              "name": "CVE-2023-45290",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45290 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When parsing a multipart form (either explicitly with Request.ParseMultipartForm or implicitly with Request.FormValue, Request.PostFormValue, or Request.FormFile), limits on the total size of the parsed form were not applied to the memory consumed while reading a single form line. This permits a maliciously crafted input containing very long lines to cause allocation of arbitrarily large amounts of memory, potentially leading to memory exhaustion. With fix, the ParseMultipartForm function now correctly limits the maximum size of form lines."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-45290",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24783",
              "name": "CVE-2024-24783",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24783 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Verifying a certificate chain which contains a certificate with an unknown public key algorithm will cause Certificate.Verify to panic. This affects all crypto/tls clients, and servers that set Config.ClientAuth to VerifyClientCertIfGiven or RequireAndVerifyClientCert. The default behavior is for TLS servers to not verify client certificates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-24783",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24784",
              "name": "CVE-2024-24784",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24784 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ParseAddressList function incorrectly handles comments (text within parentheses) within display names. Since this is a misalignment with conforming address parsers, it can result in different trust decisions being made by programs using different parsers."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-24784",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24785",
              "name": "CVE-2024-24785",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24785 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If errors returned from MarshalJSON methods contain user controlled data, they may be used to break the contextual auto-escaping behavior of the html/template package, allowing for subsequent actions to inject unexpected content into templates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-24785",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24789",
              "name": "CVE-2024-24789",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24789 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The archive/zip package's handling of certain types of invalid zip files differs from the behavior of most zip implementations. This misalignment could be exploited to create an zip file with contents that vary depending on the implementation reading the file. The archive/zip package now rejects files containing these errors."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-24789",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24791",
              "name": "CVE-2024-24791",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24791 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/http HTTP/1.1 client mishandled the case where a server responds to a request with an \"Expect: 100-continue\" header with a non-informational (200 or higher) status. This mishandling could leave a client connection in an invalid state, where the next request sent on the connection will fail. An attacker sending a request to a net/http/httputil.ReverseProxy proxy can exploit this mishandling to cause a denial of service by sending \"Expect: 100-continue\" requests which elicit a non-informational response from the backend. Each such request leaves the proxy with an invalid connection, and causes one subsequent request using that connection to fail."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-24791",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-34155",
              "name": "CVE-2024-34155",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-34155 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling any of the Parse functions on Go source code which contains deeply nested literals can cause a panic due to stack exhaustion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-34155",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-34158",
              "name": "CVE-2024-34158",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-34158 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling Parse on a \"// +build\" build tag line with deeply nested expressions can cause a panic due to stack exhaustion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-34158",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-45336",
              "name": "CVE-2024-45336",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-45336 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP client drops sensitive headers after following a cross-domain redirect. For example, a request to a.com/ containing an Authorization header which is redirected to b.com/ will not send that header to b.com. In the event that the client received a subsequent same-domain redirect, however, the sensitive headers would be restored. For example, a chain of redirects from a.com/, to b.com/1, and finally to b.com/2 would incorrectly send the Authorization header to b.com/2."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-45336",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-0913",
              "name": "CVE-2025-0913",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-0913 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|O_EXCL) behaved differently on Unix and Windows systems when the target path was a dangling symlink. On Unix systems, OpenFile with O_CREATE and O_EXCL flags never follows symlinks. On Windows, when the target path was a symlink to a nonexistent location, OpenFile would create a file in that location. OpenFile now always returns an error when the O_CREATE and O_EXCL flags are both set and the target path is a symlink."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-0913",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22866",
              "name": "CVE-2025-22866",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22866 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Due to the usage of a variable time instruction in the assembly implementation of an internal function, a small number of bits of secret scalars are leaked on the ppc64le architecture. Due to the way this function is used, we do not believe this leakage is enough to allow recovery of the private key when P-256 is used in any well known protocols."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22866",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22870",
              "name": "CVE-2025-22870",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22870 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22870",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22871",
              "name": "CVE-2025-22871",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22871 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/http package improperly accepts a bare LF as a line terminator in chunked data chunk-size lines. This can permit request smuggling if a net/http server is used in conjunction with a server that incorrectly accepts a bare LF as part of a chunk-ext."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22871",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22873",
              "name": "CVE-2025-22873",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22873 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It was possible to improperly access the parent directory of an os.Root by opening a filename ending in \"../\". For example, Root.Open(\"../\") would open the parent directory of the Root. This escape only permits opening the parent directory itself, not ancestors of the parent or files contained within the parent."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22873",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4673",
              "name": "CVE-2025-4673",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4673 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Proxy-Authorization and Proxy-Authenticate headers persisted on cross-origin redirects potentially leaking sensitive information."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-4673",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47906",
              "name": "CVE-2025-47906",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-47906 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If the PATH environment variable contains paths which are executables (rather than just directories), passing certain strings to LookPath (\"\", \".\", and \"..\"), can result in the binaries listed in the PATH being unexpectedly returned."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47906",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47907",
              "name": "CVE-2025-47907",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-47907 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Cancelling a query (e.g. by cancelling the context passed to one of the query methods) during a call to the Scan method of the returned Rows can result in unexpected results if other queries are being made in parallel. This can result in a race condition that may overwrite the expected results with those of another query, causing the call to Scan to return either unexpected results from the other query or an error."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47907",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47912",
              "name": "CVE-2025-47912",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-47912 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Parse function permits values other than IPv6 addresses to be included in square brackets within the host component of a URL. RFC 3986 permits IPv6 addresses to be included within the host component, enclosed within square brackets. For example: \"http://[::1]/\". IPv4 addresses and hostnames must not appear within square brackets. Parse did not enforce this requirement."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47912",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58183",
              "name": "CVE-2025-58183",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58183 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58183",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58185",
              "name": "CVE-2025-58185",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58185 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Parsing a maliciously crafted DER payload could allocate large amounts of memory, causing memory exhaustion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58185",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58187",
              "name": "CVE-2025-58187",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58187 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Due to the design of the name constraint checking algorithm, the processing time of some inputs scale non-linearly with respect to the size of the certificate. This affects programs which validate arbitrary certificate chains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58187",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58188",
              "name": "CVE-2025-58188",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58188 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Validating certificate chains which contain DSA public keys can cause programs to panic, due to a interface cast that assumes they implement the Equal method. This affects programs which validate arbitrary certificate chains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58188",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58189",
              "name": "CVE-2025-58189",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58189 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When Conn.Handshake fails during ALPN negotiation the error contains attacker controlled information (the ALPN protocols sent by the client) which is not escaped."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58189",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61723",
              "name": "CVE-2025-61723",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61723 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The processing time for parsing some invalid inputs scales non-linearly with respect to the size of the input. This affects programs which parse untrusted PEM inputs."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61723",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61724",
              "name": "CVE-2025-61724",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61724 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Reader.ReadResponse function constructs a response string through repeated string concatenation of lines. When the number of lines in a response is large, this can cause excessive CPU consumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61724",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61725",
              "name": "CVE-2025-61725",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61725 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ParseAddress function constructs domain-literal address components through repeated string concatenation. When parsing large domain-literal components, this can cause excessive CPU consumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61725",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61727",
              "name": "CVE-2025-61727",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61727 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An excluded subdomain constraint in a certificate chain does not restrict the usage of wildcard SANs in the leaf certificate. For example a constraint that excludes the subdomain test.example.com does not prevent a leaf certificate from claiming the SAN *.example.com."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61727",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61728",
              "name": "CVE-2025-61728",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61728 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "archive/zip uses a super-linear file name indexing algorithm that is invoked the first time a file in an archive is opened. This can lead to a denial of service when consuming a maliciously constructed ZIP archive."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61728",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61730",
              "name": "CVE-2025-61730",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61730 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During the TLS 1.3 handshake if multiple messages are sent in records that span encryption level boundaries (for instance the Client Hello and Encrypted Extensions messages), the subsequent messages may be processed before the encryption level changes. This can cause some minor information disclosure if a network-local attacker can inject messages during the handshake."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61730",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27142",
              "name": "CVE-2026-27142",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27142 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Actions which insert URLs into the content attribute of HTML meta tags are not escaped. This can allow XSS if the meta tag also has an http-equiv attribute with the value \"refresh\". A new GODEBUG setting has been added, htmlmetacontenturlescape, which can be used to disable escaping URLs in actions in the meta content attribute which follow \"url=\" by setting htmlmetacontenturlescape=0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27142",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32282",
              "name": "CVE-2026-32282",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32282 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Linux, if the target of Root.Chmod is replaced with a symlink while the chmod operation is in progress, Chmod can operate on the target of the symlink, even when the target lies outside the root. The Linux fchmodat syscall silently ignores the AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW flag, which Root.Chmod uses to avoid symlink traversal. Root.Chmod checks its target before acting and returns an error if the target is a symlink lying outside the root, so the impact is limited to cases where the target is replaced with a symlink between the check and operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32282",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32288",
              "name": "CVE-2026-32288",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32288 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tar.Reader can allocate an unbounded amount of memory when reading a maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions encoded in the \"old GNU sparse map\" format."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32288",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32289",
              "name": "CVE-2026-32289",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32289 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Context was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied. These issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32289",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39823",
              "name": "CVE-2026-39823",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39823 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27142 fixed a vulnerability in which URLs were not correctly escaped inside of a <meta> tag's <content> attribute. If the URL content were to insert ASCII whitespaces around the '=' rune inside of the <content> attribute, the escaper would fail to similarly escape it, leading to XSS."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39823",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39825",
              "name": "CVE-2026-39825",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39825 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ReverseProxy can forward queries containing parameters not visible to Rewrite functions. When used with a Rewrite function, or a Director function which parses query parameters, ReverseProxy sanitizes the forwarded request to remove query parameters which are not parsed by url.ParseQuery. ReverseProxy does not take ParseQuery's limit on the total number of query parameters (controlled by GODEBUG=urlmaxqueryparams=N) into account. This can permit ReverseProxy to forward a request containing a query parameter that is not visible to the Rewrite function. For example, the query \"a1=x&a2=x&...&a10000=x&hidden=y\" can forward the parameter \"hidden=y\" while hiding it from the proxy's Rewrite function."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39825",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39826",
              "name": "CVE-2026-39826",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39826 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If a trusted template author were to write a <script> tag containing an empty 'type' attribute or a 'type' attribute with an ASCII whitespace, the execution of the template would incorrectly escape any data passed into the <script> block."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39826",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42505",
              "name": "CVE-2026-42505",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42505 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Handshakes which used Encrypted Client Hello could be de-anonymized by a passive network observer due to a disclosure of pre-shared key identities in the unencrypted client hello."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42505",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42507",
              "name": "CVE-2026-42507",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42507 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When returning errors, functions in the net/textproto package would include its input as part of the error. This might allow an attacker to inject misleading content to errors that are printed or logged."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42507",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2022-1144",
              "name": "GO-2022-1144",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2022-1144 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker can cause excessive memory growth in a Go server accepting HTTP/2 requests.\n\nHTTP/2 server connections contain a cache of HTTP header keys sent by the client. While the total number of entries in this cache is capped, an attacker sending very large keys can cause the server to allocate approximately 64 MiB per open connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/56350",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-1878",
              "name": "GO-2023-1878",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-1878 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP/1 client does not fully validate the contents of the Host header. A maliciously crafted Host header can inject additional headers or entire requests.\n\nWith fix, the HTTP/1 client now refuses to send requests containing an invalid Request.Host or Request.URL.Host value."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/60374",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-1987",
              "name": "GO-2023-1987",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-1987 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Extremely large RSA keys in certificate chains can cause a client/server to expend significant CPU time verifying signatures.\n\nWith fix, the size of RSA keys transmitted during handshakes is restricted to <= 8192 bits.\n\nBased on a survey of publicly trusted RSA keys, there are currently only three certificates in circulation with keys larger than this, and all three appear to be test certificates that are not actively deployed. It is possible there are larger keys in use in private PKIs, but we target the web PKI, so causing breakage here in the interests of increasing the default safety of users of crypto/tls seems reasonable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/61460",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-2599",
              "name": "GO-2024-2599",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2024-2599 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When parsing a multipart form (either explicitly with Request.ParseMultipartForm or implicitly with Request.FormValue, Request.PostFormValue, or Request.FormFile), limits on the total size of the parsed form were not applied to the memory consumed while reading a single form line. This permits a maliciously crafted input containing very long lines to cause allocation of arbitrarily large amounts of memory, potentially leading to memory exhaustion.\n\nWith fix, the ParseMultipartForm function now correctly limits the maximum size of form lines."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/65383",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2022-0525",
              "name": "GO-2022-0525",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2022-0525 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP/1 client accepted some invalid Transfer-Encoding headers as indicating a \"chunked\" encoding. This could potentially allow for request smuggling, but only if combined with an intermediate server that also improperly failed to reject the header as invalid."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/409874",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2022-0520",
              "name": "GO-2022-0520",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2022-0520 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Client IP adresses may be unintentionally exposed via X-Forwarded-For headers.\n\nWhen httputil.ReverseProxy.ServeHTTP is called with a Request.Header map containing a nil value for the X-Forwarded-For header, ReverseProxy sets the client IP as the value of the X-Forwarded-For header, contrary to its documentation.\n\nIn the more usual case where a Director function sets the X-Forwarded-For header value to nil, ReverseProxy leaves the header unmodified as expected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/412857",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-2382",
              "name": "GO-2023-2382",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-2382 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A malicious HTTP sender can use chunk extensions to cause a receiver reading from a request or response body to read many more bytes from the network than are in the body.\n\nA malicious HTTP client can further exploit this to cause a server to automatically read a large amount of data (up to about 1GiB) when a handler fails to read the entire body of a request.\n\nChunk extensions are a little-used HTTP feature which permit including additional metadata in a request or response body sent using the chunked encoding. The net/http chunked encoding reader discards this metadata. A sender can exploit this by inserting a large metadata segment with each byte transferred. The chunk reader now produces an error if the ratio of real body to encoded bytes grows too small."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/64433",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-2600",
              "name": "GO-2024-2600",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2024-2600 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When following an HTTP redirect to a domain which is not a subdomain match or exact match of the initial domain, an http.Client does not forward sensitive headers such as \"Authorization\" or \"Cookie\". For example, a redirect from foo.com to www.foo.com will forward the Authorization header, but a redirect to bar.com will not.\n\nA maliciously crafted HTTP redirect could cause sensitive headers to be unexpectedly forwarded."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/65065",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-2186",
              "name": "GO-2023-2186",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-2186 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Windows, The IsLocal function does not correctly detect reserved device names in some cases.\n\nReserved names followed by spaces, such as \"COM1 \", and reserved names \"COM\" and \"LPT\" followed by superscript 1, 2, or 3, are incorrectly reported as local.\n\nWith fix, IsLocal now correctly reports these names as non-local."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/63713",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2022-0515",
              "name": "GO-2022-0515",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2022-0515 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling any of the Parse functions on Go source code which contains deeply nested types or declarations can cause a panic due to stack exhaustion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/417063",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-2041",
              "name": "GO-2023-2041",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-2041 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The html/template package does not properly handle HTML-like \"\" comment tokens, nor hashbang \"#!\" comment tokens, in <script> contexts. This may cause the template parser to improperly interpret the contents of <script> contexts, causing actions to be improperly escaped. This may be leveraged to perform an XSS attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/62196",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-2043",
              "name": "GO-2023-2043",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-2043 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The html/template package does not apply the proper rules for handling occurrences of \"<script\", \"<!--\", and \"</script\" within JS literals in <script> contexts. This may cause the template parser to improperly consider script contexts to be terminated early, causing actions to be improperly escaped. This could be leveraged to perform an XSS attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/62197",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2023-1621",
              "name": "GO-2023-1621",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2023-1621 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ScalarMult and ScalarBaseMult methods of the P256 Curve may return an incorrect result if called with some specific unreduced scalars (a scalar larger than the order of the curve).\n\nThis does not impact usages of crypto/ecdsa or crypto/ecdh."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/58647",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-2610",
              "name": "GO-2024-2610",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2024-2610 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If errors returned from MarshalJSON methods contain user controlled data, they may be used to break the contextual auto-escaping behavior of the html/template package, allowing for subsequent actions to inject unexpected content into templates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/65697",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-3105",
              "name": "GO-2024-3105",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2024-3105 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling any of the Parse functions on Go source code which contains deeply nested literals can cause a panic due to stack exhaustion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/611238",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4342",
              "name": "GO-2026-4342",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4342 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "archive/zip uses a super-linear file name indexing algorithm that is invoked the first time a file in an archive is opened. This can lead to a denial of service when consuming a maliciously constructed ZIP archive."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/736713",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3420",
              "name": "GO-2025-3420",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3420 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP client drops sensitive headers after following a cross-domain redirect. For example, a request to a.com/ containing an Authorization header which is redirected to b.com/ will not send that header to b.com.\n\nIn the event that the client received a subsequent same-domain redirect, however, the sensitive headers would be restored. For example, a chain of redirects from a.com/, to b.com/1, and finally to b.com/2 would incorrectly send the Authorization header to b.com/2."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/643100",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-2598",
              "name": "GO-2024-2598",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2024-2598 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Verifying a certificate chain which contains a certificate with an unknown public key algorithm will cause Certificate.Verify to panic.\n\nThis affects all crypto/tls clients, and servers that set Config.ClientAuth to VerifyClientCertIfGiven or RequireAndVerifyClientCert. The default behavior is for TLS servers to not verify client certificates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/65390",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3751",
              "name": "GO-2025-3751",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3751 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Proxy-Authorization and Proxy-Authenticate headers persisted on cross-origin redirects potentially leaking sensitive information."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/679257",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3956",
              "name": "GO-2025-3956",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3956 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If the PATH environment variable contains paths which are executables (rather than just directories), passing certain strings to LookPath (\"\", \".\", and \"..\"), can result in the binaries listed in the PATH being unexpectedly returned."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/691775",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4012",
              "name": "GO-2025-4012",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4012 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Despite HTTP headers having a default limit of 1MB, the number of cookies that can be parsed does not have a limit. By sending a lot of very small cookies such as \"a=;\", an attacker can make an HTTP server allocate a large amount of structs, causing large memory consumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/75672",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4011",
              "name": "GO-2025-4011",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4011 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Parsing a maliciously crafted DER payload could allocate large amounts of memory, causing memory exhaustion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/75671",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4015",
              "name": "GO-2025-4015",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4015 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Reader.ReadResponse function constructs a response string through repeated string concatenation of lines. When the number of lines in a response is large, this can cause excessive CPU consumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/709859",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3373",
              "name": "GO-2025-3373",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3373 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A certificate with a URI which has a IPv6 address with a zone ID may incorrectly satisfy a URI name constraint that applies to the certificate chain.\n\nCertificates containing URIs are not permitted in the web PKI, so this only affects users of private PKIs which make use of URIs."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/643099",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2024-2888",
              "name": "GO-2024-2888",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2024-2888 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The archive/zip package's handling of certain types of invalid zip files differs from the behavior of most zip implementations. This misalignment could be exploited to create an zip file with contents that vary depending on the implementation reading the file. The archive/zip package now rejects files containing these errors."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/585397",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4008",
              "name": "GO-2025-4008",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4008 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When Conn.Handshake fails during ALPN negotiation the error contains attacker controlled information (the ALPN protocols sent by the client) which is not escaped."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/707776",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4010",
              "name": "GO-2025-4010",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4010 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Parse function permits values other than IPv6 addresses to be included in square brackets within the host component of a URL. RFC 3986 permits IPv6 addresses to be included within the host component, enclosed within square brackets. For example: \"http://[::1]/\". IPv4 addresses and hostnames must not appear within square brackets. Parse did not enforce this requirement."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/75678",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4980",
              "name": "GO-2026-4980",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4980 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If a trusted template author were to write a <script> tag containing an empty 'type' attribute or a 'type' attribute with an ASCII whitespace, the execution of the template would incorrectly escape any data passed into the <script> block."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/78981",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4976",
              "name": "GO-2026-4976",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4976 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ReverseProxy can forward queries containing parameters not visible to Rewrite functions.\n\nWhen used with a Rewrite function, or a Director function which parses query parameters, ReverseProxy sanitizes the forwarded request to remove query parameters which are not parsed by url.ParseQuery. ReverseProxy does not take ParseQuery's limit on the total number of query parameters (controlled by GODEBUG=urlmaxqueryparams=N) into account. This can permit ReverseProxy to forward a request containing a query parameter that is not visible to the Rewrite function.\n\nFor example, the query \"a1=x&a2=x&...&a10000=x&hidden=y\" can forward the parameter \"hidden=y\" while hiding it from the proxy's Rewrite function."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/770541",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4014",
              "name": "GO-2025-4014",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4014 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/709861",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5039",
              "name": "GO-2026-5039",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-5039 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When returning errors, functions in the net/textproto package would include its input as part of the error. This might allow an attacker to inject misleading content to errors that are printed or logged."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/79346",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4603",
              "name": "GO-2026-4603",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4603 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Actions which insert URLs into the content attribute of HTML meta tags are not escaped. This can allow XSS if the meta tag also has an http-equiv attribute with the value \"refresh\".\n\nA new GODEBUG setting has been added, htmlmetacontenturlescape, which can be used to disable escaping URLs in actions in the meta content attribute which follow \"url=\" by setting htmlmetacontenturlescape=0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/EdhZqrQ98hk",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3503",
              "name": "GO-2025-3503",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3503 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/654697",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4982",
              "name": "GO-2026-4982",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4982 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27142 fixed a vulnerability in which URLs were not correctly escaped inside of a <meta> tag's <content> attribute. If the URL content were to insert ASCII whitespaces around the '=' rune inside of the <content> attribute, the escaper would fail to similarly escape it, leading to XSS."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/78913",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4864",
              "name": "GO-2026-4864",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4864 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Linux, if the target of Root.Chmod is replaced with a symlink while the chmod operation is in progress, Chmod can operate on the target of the symlink, even when the target lies outside the root.\n\nThe Linux fchmodat syscall silently ignores the AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW flag, which Root.Chmod uses to avoid symlink traversal. Root.Chmod checks its target before acting and returns an error if the target is a symlink lying outside the root, so the impact is limited to cases where the target is replaced with a symlink between the check and operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/763761",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-4175",
              "name": "GO-2025-4175",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-4175 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An excluded subdomain constraint in a certificate chain does not restrict the usage of wildcard SANs in the leaf certificate. For example a constraint that excludes the subdomain test.example.com does not prevent a leaf certificate from claiming the SAN *.example.com."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/723900",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4865",
              "name": "GO-2026-4865",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4865 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Context was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied.\n\nThese issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/763762",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4869",
              "name": "GO-2026-4869",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4869 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tar.Reader can allocate an unbounded amount of memory when reading a maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions encoded in the \"old GNU sparse map\" format."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/763766",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4340",
              "name": "GO-2026-4340",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4340 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During the TLS 1.3 handshake if multiple messages are sent in records that span encryption level boundaries (for instance the Client Hello and Encrypted Extensions messages), the subsequent messages may be processed before the encryption level changes. This can cause some minor information disclosure if a network-local attacker can inject messages during the handshake."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/724120",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5856",
              "name": "GO-2026-5856",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-5856 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Handshakes which used Encrypted Client Hello could be de-anonymized by a passive network observer due to a disclosure of pre-shared key identities in the unencrypted client hello."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/775960",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3750",
              "name": "GO-2025-3750",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3750 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|O_EXCL) behaved differently on Unix and Windows systems when the target path was a dangling symlink. On Unix systems, OpenFile with O_CREATE and O_EXCL flags never follows symlinks. On Windows, when the target path was a symlink to a nonexistent location, OpenFile would create a file in that location. OpenFile now always returns an error when the O_CREATE and O_EXCL flags are both set and the target path is a symlink."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/672396",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2025-3447",
              "name": "GO-2025-3447",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2025-3447 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Due to the usage of a variable time instruction in the assembly implementation of an internal function, a small number of bits of secret scalars are leaked on the ppc64le architecture. Due to the way this function is used, we do not believe this leakage is enough to allow recovery of the private key when P-256 is used in any well known protocols."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/643735",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
