            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41256",
              "name": "CVE-2026-41256",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41256 in jq"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "jq is a command-line JSON processor. In 1.8.1 and earlier, Top-level jq programs loaded from a file with -f are truncated at the first embedded NUL byte on current upstream HEAD. A crafted filter file such as . followed by \\x00 and arbitrary suffix compiles and executes as only the prefix before the NUL. This leaves jq with a post-CVE-2026-33948 prefix/full-buffer mismatch on the compilation path even though the JSON parser path has already been fixed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41256",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41257",
              "name": "CVE-2026-41257",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41257 in jq"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "jq is a command-line JSON processor. In 1.8.1 and earlier, the jq bytecode VM's data stack tracks its allocation size in a signed int. When the stack grows beyond ≈1 GiB (via deeply nested generator forks), the doubling arithmetic overflows. The wrapped value is passed to realloc and then used for a memmove with attacker-influenced offsets."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41257",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43895",
              "name": "CVE-2026-43895",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-43895 in jq"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "jq is a command-line JSON processor. In 1.8.1 and earlier, jq accepts embedded NUL bytes in import paths at the jq-language level, but later resolves those paths through C string operations during module and data-file lookup. This creates a mismatch between the logical import string that policy or audit code may validate and the on-disk path that jq actually opens."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43895",
