            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59729",
              "name": "CVE-2025-59729",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-59729 in ffmpeg"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When parsing the header for a DHAV file, there's an integer underflow in offset calculation that leads to reading the duration from before the start of the allocated buffer.\n\nIf we load a DHAV file that is larger than MAX_DURATION_BUFFER_SIZE bytes (0x100000) for example 0x101000 bytes, then at [0] we have size = 0x101000. At [1] we have end_buffer_size = 0x100000, and at [2] we have end_buffer_pos = 0x1000.\n\nThe loop then scans backwards through the buffer looking for the dhav tag; when it is found, we'll calculate end_pos based on a 32-bit offset read from the buffer.\n\nThere is subsequently a check [3] that end_pos is within the section of the file that has been copied into end_buffer, but it only correctly handles the cases where end_pos is before the start of the file or after the section copied into end_buffer, and not the case where end_pos is within the the file, but before the section copied into end_buffer. If we provide such an offset, (end_pos - end_buffer_pos) can underflow, resulting in the subsequent access at [4] occurring before the beginning of the allocation.\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59729",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59730",
              "name": "CVE-2025-59730",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-59730 in ffmpeg"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When decoding a frame for a SANM file (ANIM v0 variant), the decoded data can be larger than the buffer allocated for it.\n\nFrames encoded with codec 48 can specify their resolution (width x height). A buffer of appropriate size is allocated depending on the resolution.\n\nThis codec can encode the frame contents using a run-length encoding algorithm. There are no checks that the decoded frame fits in the allocated buffer, leading to a heap-buffer-overflow.\n\nprocess_frame_obj initializes the buffers based on the frame resolution:\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59730",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "medium"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-qmgc-5h2g-mvrw",
              "name": "GHSA-qmgc-5h2g-mvrw",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GHSA-qmgc-5h2g-mvrw in filelock"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "filelock Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) Symlink Vulnerability in SoftFileLock"
              },
