            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-0563",
              "name": "CVE-2022-0563",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-0563 in bsdutils"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the util-linux chfn and chsh utilities when compiled with Readline support. The Readline library uses an \"INPUTRC\" environment variable to get a path to the library config file. When the library cannot parse the specified file, it prints an error message containing data from the file. This flaw allows an unprivileged user to read root-owned files, potentially leading to privilege escalation. This flaw affects util-linux versions prior to 2.37.4."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-0563",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-14104",
              "name": "CVE-2025-14104",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-14104 in bsdutils"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. This vulnerability allows a heap buffer overread when processing 256-byte usernames, specifically within the `setpwnam()` function, affecting SUID (Set User ID) login-utils utilities writing to the password database."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-14104",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-18018",
              "name": "CVE-2017-18018",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-18018 in coreutils"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In GNU Coreutils through 8.29, chown-core.c in chown and chgrp does not prevent replacement of a plain file with a symlink during use of the POSIX \"-R -L\" options, which allows local users to modify the ownership of arbitrary files by leveraging a race condition."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2017-18018",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-5278",
              "name": "CVE-2025-5278",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-5278 in coreutils"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
