                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-30629",
              "name": "CVE-2022-30629",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-30629 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Non-random values for ticket_age_add in session tickets in crypto/tls before Go 1.17.11 and Go 1.18.3 allow an attacker that can observe TLS handshakes to correlate successive connections by comparing ticket ages during session resumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-30629",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-45341",
              "name": "CVE-2024-45341",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-45341 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A certificate with a URI which has a IPv6 address with a zone ID may incorrectly satisfy a URI name constraint that applies to the certificate chain. Certificates containing URIs are not permitted in the web PKI, so this only affects users of private PKIs which make use of URIs."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-45341",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58186",
              "name": "CVE-2025-58186",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58186 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Despite HTTP headers having a default limit of 1MB, the number of cookies that can be parsed does not have a limit. By sending a lot of very small cookies such as \"a=;\", an attacker can make an HTTP server allocate a large amount of structs, causing large memory consumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58186",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27139",
              "name": "CVE-2026-27139",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27139 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2022-0531",
              "name": "GO-2022-0531",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2022-0531 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker can correlate a resumed TLS session with a previous connection.\n\nSession tickets generated by crypto/tls do not contain a randomly generated ticket_age_add, which allows an attacker that can observe TLS handshakes to correlate successive connections by comparing ticket ages during session resumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/405994",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4403",
              "name": "GO-2026-4403",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4403 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It was possible to improperly access the parent directory of an os.Root by opening a filename ending in \"../\". For example, Root.Open(\"../\") would open the parent directory of the Root. This escape only permits opening the parent directory itself, not ancestors of the parent or files contained within the parent."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/670036",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-4602",
              "name": "GO-2026-4602",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-4602 in stdlib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened.\n\nThe impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/EdhZqrQ98hk",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5024",
              "name": "GO-2026-5024",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GO-2026-5024 in golang.org/x/sys"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "NewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/78916",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "low"
                ]
              }
            },
