            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-46246",
              "name": "CVE-2023-46246",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-46246 in vim"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vim is an improved version of the good old UNIX editor Vi. Heap-use-after-free in memory allocated in the function `ga_grow_inner` in in the file `src/alloc.c` at line 748, which is freed in the file `src/ex_docmd.c` in the function `do_cmdline` at line 1010 and then used again in `src/cmdhist.c` at line 759. When using the `:history` command, it's possible that the provided argument overflows the accepted value. Causing an Integer Overflow and potentially later an use-after-free. This vulnerability has been patched in version 9.0.2068."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-46246",
